Feature: Compound Drug Analysis Aggregation and Potential Categorization

  This feature performs compound screening analysis on the purgo_playground.compound_drug_analysis table, including filtering, aggregation, joining, and result categorization based on overall_score.

  Background:
    Given the source table is "purgo_playground.compound_drug_analysis" in Unity Catalog "purgo_databricks" schema "purgo_playground"
    And the table contains columns: study_id, compound_id, mutation_id, therapeutic_area, drug_name, ic50, auc, efficacy, toxicity, potency, sample_size, mutation_frequency, mutation_severity, compound_concentration, cell_viability, growth_inhibition, result, approved_flag, validation_status, status, created_by, score1, score2, score3, score4, score5

  # Happy Path: Valid Filtering, Aggregation, Join, and Categorization

  Scenario: Filter, aggregate, join, and categorize compound drug analysis data
    Given the compound_drug_analysis table contains rows with approved_flag = 1 and validation_status = "valid"
    When the data is filtered to include only rows where approved_flag = 1 and validation_status = "valid"
    And the filtered data is grouped by therapeutic_area to calculate:
      | avg_ic50         | average of ic50 (double, nullable)           |
      | avg_auc          | average of auc (double, nullable)            |
      | avg_efficacy     | average of efficacy (double, nullable)       |
      | total_sample_size| sum of sample_size (bigint, nullable)        |
      | study_count      | count of study_id (string, nullable)         |
    And the filtered data is joined with the aggregated data on therapeutic_area
    And for each row, overall_score is calculated as the mean of score1, score2, score3, score4, score5, ignoring nulls
    And each row is categorized as:
      | High Potential     | overall_score >= 70 and <= 100 |
      | Moderate Potential | overall_score >= 60 and < 70   |
      | Low Potential      | overall_score < 60             |
    Then the final output includes all columns from compound_drug_analysis plus avg_ic50, avg_auc, avg_efficacy, total_sample_size, study_count, overall_score, and potential_category

  # Error Scenario: Filtering with No Valid Rows

  Scenario: No rows match filter criteria
    Given the compound_drug_analysis table contains no rows where approved_flag = 1 and validation_status = "valid"
    When the data is filtered to include only rows where approved_flag = 1 and validation_status = "valid"
    Then the output is an empty result set

  # Error Scenario: Invalid Data Types

  Scenario Outline: Invalid data types in critical columns
    Given the compound_drug_analysis table contains a row with <column> value as <invalid_value>
    When the data is processed for aggregation and scoring
    Then an error is raised with message "<error_message>"

    Examples:
      | column      | invalid_value | error_message                                      |
      | ic50        | "abc"         | "Invalid data type for ic50: expected double"      |
      | auc         | "xyz"         | "Invalid data type for auc: expected double"       |
      | efficacy    | "none"        | "Invalid data type for efficacy: expected double"  |
      | sample_size | "ten"         | "Invalid data type for sample_size: expected bigint"|
      | score1      | "NaN"         | "Invalid data type for score1: expected double"    |

  # Error Scenario: Null or Missing Scores

  Scenario Outline: Calculation of overall_score with missing/null scores
    Given a row in compound_drug_analysis with score1=<score1>, score2=<score2>, score3=<score3>, score4=<score4>, score5=<score5>
    When overall_score is calculated as the mean of available (non-null) scores
    Then overall_score is <expected_score>
    And potential_category is assigned based on overall_score

    Examples:
      | score1 | score2 | score3 | score4 | score5 | expected_score | potential_category   |
      | 80     | 90     | 85     | 75     | 95     | 85             | High Potential      |
      | 65     | 70     | null   | 60     | 65     | 65             | Moderate Potential  |
      | 55     | null   | null   | 50     | 45     | 50             | Low Potential       |
      | null   | null   | null   | null   | null   | null           | null                |

  # Error Scenario: Out-of-Range Score Values

  Scenario Outline: Score values outside valid range
    Given a row in compound_drug_analysis with score1=<score1>, score2=<score2>, score3=<score3>, score4=<score4>, score5=<score5>
    When overall_score is calculated
    Then an error is raised with message "Score value out of valid range (0-100)"

    Examples:
      | score1 | score2 | score3 | score4 | score5 |
      | 120    | 90     | 85     | 75     | 95     |
      | -10    | 70     | 65     | 60     | 65     |

  # Data-Driven Test: Aggregation and Categorization by Therapeutic Area

  Scenario Outline: Aggregation and categorization for multiple therapeutic areas
    Given the compound_drug_analysis table contains rows for therapeutic_area "<therapeutic_area>" with ic50 values <ic50_list>, auc values <auc_list>, efficacy values <efficacy_list>, sample_size values <sample_size_list>, and study_ids <study_id_list>
    When the data is grouped by therapeutic_area
    Then avg_ic50 is <expected_avg_ic50>
    And avg_auc is <expected_avg_auc>
    And avg_efficacy is <expected_avg_efficacy>
    And total_sample_size is <expected_total_sample_size>
    And study_count is <expected_study_count>

    Examples:
      | therapeutic_area | ic50_list      | auc_list       | efficacy_list   | sample_size_list | study_id_list      | expected_avg_ic50 | expected_avg_auc | expected_avg_efficacy | expected_total_sample_size | expected_study_count |
      | Oncology        | 50,60,70       | 200,220,210    | 80,85,90        | 100,120,110      | S1,S2,S3           | 60                | 210              | 85                    | 330                      | 3                   |
      | Cardiology      | 40,45          | 180,190        | 70,75           | 90,95            | S4,S5              | 42.5              | 185              | 72.5                  | 185                      | 2                   |

  # Error Scenario: Duplicate Therapeutic Area Mapping

  Scenario: Compound maps to multiple therapeutic areas
    Given a compound_id maps to multiple therapeutic_area values in compound_drug_analysis
    When the data is grouped by therapeutic_area
    Then the compound is included in each therapeutic_area group for aggregation and categorization

  # Error Scenario: Join Failure

  Scenario: Join fails due to missing therapeutic_area in aggregated data
    Given a row in filtered compound_drug_analysis with therapeutic_area "RareDisease" not present in aggregated data
    When the join is performed on therapeutic_area
    Then the row is excluded from the final output

  # Error Scenario: Large Data Volume

  Scenario: Data volume exceeds processing threshold
    Given the compound_drug_analysis table contains more than 10 million rows
    When the analysis is executed
    Then the process completes successfully within acceptable performance limits

  # Error Scenario: Missing Required Columns

  Scenario Outline: Missing required columns in source table
    Given the compound_drug_analysis table is missing column <missing_column>
    When the analysis is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Missing required column: <missing_column>"

    Examples:
      | missing_column |
      | ic50          |
      | auc           |
      | efficacy      |
      | sample_size   |
      | score1        |
      | score2        |
      | score3        |
      | score4        |
      | score5        |

  # Error Scenario: Invalid Approved Flag or Validation Status

  Scenario Outline: Invalid values for approved_flag or validation_status
    Given a row in compound_drug_analysis with approved_flag=<approved_flag> and validation_status=<validation_status>
    When the data is filtered
    Then the row is excluded from the analysis

    Examples:
      | approved_flag | validation_status |
      | 0             | valid            |
      | 1             | invalid          |
      | 0             | invalid          |
      | null          | valid            |
      | 1             | null             |

  # Error Scenario: Output Schema Validation

  Scenario: Output includes all required columns
    Given the final output is generated
    When the output schema is validated
    Then the output includes all columns from compound_drug_analysis plus avg_ic50, avg_auc, avg_efficacy, total_sample_size, study_count, overall_score, and potential_category

